       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily, and usual doses are 2.5 to 10 mg. 50 mg is five times that maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. This patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in their profile explains a higher dose.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a common starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, a lower starting dose, sometimes used in frail patients\n\nIf 50 mg is what you intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. I'd recommend checking with pharmacy first. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter the order right away."
